01:00:10,588 --> 01:00:16,588
The Toolbox Murders is a 1978 American slasher film directed by Dennis Donnelly,
from a screenplay by Neva Friedenn, Robert Easter, and Anne Kindberg.

12
01:05:38,823 --> 01:05:44,823
Starring Cameron Mitchell, Pamelyn Ferdin, and Wesley Eure, it follows a series of violent murders centered around a Los
Angeles apartment complex, followed by the kidnapping and disappearance of a teenage girl who resides there.

13
01:11:07,058 --> 01:11:13,058
The film was marketed as being a dramatization of true
events, though no source can confirm this.

14
01:16:35,294 --> 01:16:41,294
It was briefly banned in the early 1980s in the United
Kingdom during the "video nasty" panic.

15
01:22:03,529 --> 01:22:09,529
The film explores themes of tools, murder, slasher, drill, video nasty.

16
01:27:31,764 --> 01:27:37,764
The tone is intense and dark and thought_provoking.
